---
const story = 'Othala at a glance, in nine steps: 1, members open an app in a browser, through the edge, Caddy, which stands in front of every app; 2, the edge proxies to an app that speaks OIDC; 3, the app redirects them to Hydra to authorize; 4, Hydra hands the login and consent challenges to the portal; 5, the portal checks their passkey session with Kratos; 6, Hydra issues the app an id_token carrying their groups; 7, for an app without OIDC, the edge first asks the portal to allow or deny the request; 8, the edge proxies it only if allowed; 9, admins manage people on the portal\'s admin listener over the internal network, never through the edge.';
